---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const repositoryUrl = 'https://github.com/andreagrandi/draftomen';
const releaseUrl = 'https://github.com/andreagrandi/draftomen/releases/latest';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Draft Omen — A clearer signal for MTG Arena drafts"
  description="Draft Omen is a local, read-only assistant for MTG Arena Quick Drafts. It reads Player.log, explains each pick, and suggests a 40-card build."
  canonicalPath="/"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Local draft intelligence</p>
        <h1>Draft with a <span>clearer signal.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">
          Draft Omen reads Arena's local <code>Player.log</code>, ranks each pack
          with visible data, and helps turn a completed pool into a playable deck.
        </p>
        <div class="download-group" aria-label="Download Draft Omen">
          <a class="btn btn-primary download-button" href={releaseUrl}>
            <span aria-hidden="true">⌘</span>
            <span>Download for macOS<small>Latest release</small></span>
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary download-button" href={releaseUrl}>
            <span aria-hidden="true">⊞</span>
            <span>Download for Windows<small>Latest release</small></span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="install-note">
          Choose the matching OS asset on GitHub. Prefer the terminal? See the{" "}
          <a href="/docs/">setup and mechanism docs</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-art">
        <img
          src="/images/draft-omen-banner.webp"
          alt="Draft Omen logo: an eye inside a card frame beside the Draft Omen wordmark"
          width="2172"
          height="724"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Built for the pick in front of you</p>
          <h2 id="why-heading">Useful context, without the black box.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          A focused companion for Quick Draft: local-first, read-only, and honest
          about where every recommendation comes from.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="card feature-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
            <h3>Reads the log</h3>
            <p>Follows complete Arena Player.log lines instead of reading the screen or automating input.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card feature-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
            <h3>Shows the inputs</h3>
            <p>Keep raw 17Lands GIH win rate, grade, source, ALSA, and the pool-aware score in view.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card feature-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
            <h3>Stays open early</h3>
            <p>Color fit ramps from open picks toward a supported pair, with a deliberately conservative splash policy.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card feature-card">
          <div class="card-body">
            <span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
            <h3>Builds to 40</h3>
            <p>After the draft, a staged suggestion starts with 23 spells and 17 lands, then explains any compromises.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="views-heading">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">See the reasoning</p>
          <h2 id="views-heading">A draft view that stays legible.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Live Draft and Suggested deck views keep recommendations, source data, and
          options together.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="showcase-grid">
        <figure class="showcase-card">
          <img
            src="/images/draft-omen-pick-view.webp"
            alt="Draft Omen Live Draft screen: Pack 1, Pick 3 with 12 cards available, Glóin the Mighty selected, ranked card rows, DO Score, 17Lands win rate, grade, color fit, focused-card details, and pool summary"
            width="1920"
            height="1023"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Live Draft</strong>
            <span>Pack 1, Pick 3 with pool-aware ranking, focused-card details, and live pool summary.</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="showcase-card">
          <img
            src="/images/draft-omen-deck-view.webp"
            alt="Draft Omen Suggested deck screen: automatic UR pair, 40-card deck with 23 spells and 17 lands, mana base, mana curve, grouped main-deck spells, and Tidings of War selected"
            width="1920"
            height="1022"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Suggested deck</strong>
            <span>Review the automatic UR build, mana base, curve, spell groups, and selected-card details.</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-muted" aria-label="Learn more">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Want the mechanism, not a marketing promise?</strong><br />
          Read how Player.log events, ratings fallbacks, color fit, and deck
          constraints are handled in the repository docs.{" "}
          <a class="text-link" href={repositoryUrl}>View source on GitHub ↗</a>
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/docs/">Read the docs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
